From 7c51b76e52db0308850513630b942b63a81772f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 20:34:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Audit 2026-09-04: refuse non-English RFQs, keep clarification
 context, unblock the event loop, harden price entry, fix SFP28 parsing

- new_path/service.py: NON_ENGLISH_INPUT guard (Cyrillic text used to yield a
  silently reduced, approvable plan); looks_like_full_rfq needs two independent
  signals so short clarification answers no longer restart the request; public
  entry points serialised with an RLock.
- bot/handlers.py: planner calls run via asyncio.to_thread; price parsing
  handles thousands/decimal separators and accepts only price-shaped messages;
  a new RFQ typed while a price is pending starts a fresh request; stale
  /start and /quote copy.
- parsing/extractors/network.py: sfp28 before sfp\+? so 25GbE SFP28 is not
  normalised to SFP+ and rejected on every platform.
- catalog/labels.py: NIC speed accepts "2x25G" spelling (catalog must be
  regenerated with the real workbook).
- main.py: clear startup error when the configurator workbook is missing.
- Dockerfile/docker-compose: drop the non-existent templates directory.
- docs/AUDIT_2026-09-04.md: findings, fixes, open items; CLAUDE.md pointer.
- tests/test_audit_2026_09_regressions.py: 40 workbook-free regressions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
